sessionalHymns.text:
Beyond understanding and unapproachable is the dread mystery
of God wrought in thee, O divinely joyous sovereign Lady;
for having conceived the Infinite One,
thou didst give birth to Him, clad in the flesh taken from thy most pure blood.
Him do thou ever entreat as thy Son, O pure one,
that our souls be saved.

ode4.irmos2:
O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation;
I have considered Thy works,//
and I have glorified Thy Divinity.

ode5.irmos2:
Rising early we cry to Thee, O Lord;
save us, for Thou art our God,//
and we know none other besides Thee.

ode8.irmos:
Having spread his hands, Daniel closed the lions' jaws in their den;
while the zealously pious youths, girded with virtue,
quenched the power of the fire and cried aloud://
Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord.
